1
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:26,860
Aiming for the sunset
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:28,280 --> 00:00:34,000
I kicked a pebble and my shoes flew off too,

3
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:42,240
right onto the head of a
carpenter who was chopping away,

4
00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:48,440
and everyone laughed
that I'm still just a kid.

5
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:55,280
Even if I stir up some energy somewhere,
Katsushika is a place to stay.

6
00:00:55,280 --> 00:01:02,540
With a yawn, the streets stay unchanged,
and somehow they feel so gentle.

7
00:01:03,780 --> 00:01:16,820
From the pointed-hat water tower,
the sun sinks down over the natural scenery.

8
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:25,260
Tomorrow will end just like this, won't it?

9
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:29,060
Katsushika Shibamata,
happiness again, they say.

10
00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:31,760
Only after losing it did I realize.

11
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:33,960
Because I'm such a fool.

12
00:01:38,260 --> 00:01:41,620
In this world we pass through,
full of summer energy.

13
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:48,780
What?

14
00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:52,000
What do you mean,
"what"? We had a promise today, didn't we?

15
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:53,300
Uguisu, 50 of them.

16
00:01:53,540 --> 00:01:54,700
No way, that's ridiculous.

17
00:01:56,820 --> 00:01:57,860
It's today.

18
00:01:59,020 --> 00:02:01,060
You didn't forget, did you?

19
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:02,960
I've already paid for it, you know.

20
00:02:03,340 --> 00:02:05,160
Of course I didn't forget.

21
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:06,800
It's all made, don't worry.

22
00:02:07,180 --> 00:02:09,500
I see. Then I'll come
pick it up this evening.

23
00:02:10,140 --> 00:02:10,860
Hey, wait a sec.

24
00:02:12,760 --> 00:02:13,380
Uh-oh.

25
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:18,240
I don't have time for this.

26
00:02:22,360 --> 00:02:24,240
It's really coming down now.

27
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:27,700
Senpai, what are you doing, senpai?

28
00:02:28,300 --> 00:02:29,820
I'm bending bamboo strips.

29
00:02:30,460 --> 00:02:35,240
Anyone can see that. I'm asking what you're
going to do with the bent bamboo strips.

30
00:02:35,240 --> 00:02:37,500
I'm making a cage for a bush warbler.

31
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:41,680
I completely forgot the favor the
bird shop owner asked of me last month.

32
00:02:43,380 --> 00:02:45,020
Like one of those bird cages, right?

33
00:02:45,860 --> 00:02:50,000
Idiot! What I'm making isn't
some cheap junk like that!

34
00:02:51,140 --> 00:02:51,740
This one.

35
00:02:54,220 --> 00:02:56,360
I made one for an acquaintance before,

36
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:59,380
and the bird shop owner
saw it and really liked it.

37
00:02:59,380 --> 00:03:01,640
I promised to make ten of them.

38
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:02,760
For 500,000 yen.

39
00:03:02,760 --> 00:03:04,500
That much?

40
00:03:04,740 --> 00:03:06,200
That's 50,000 yen each, you know.

41
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:09,240
This takes a considerable amount of skill,
you know.

42
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:11,200
Even 50,000 is cheap.

43
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:15,000
Where? It's just bending bamboo strips
you've heated over a fire, right?

44
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:16,520
Yeah! Then go ahead and try it!

45
00:03:17,440 --> 00:03:19,980
Fine. Easy, easy.

46
00:03:24,240 --> 00:03:27,240
See? It's not as easy as it looks.

47
00:03:27,580 --> 00:03:29,136
Hah, move, move.

48
00:03:29,186 --> 00:03:32,720
I still have to make nine more by evening.

49
00:03:34,440 --> 00:03:38,040
But at this rate, bending them one by one,

50
00:03:38,040 --> 00:03:40,320
there's no way I'll make it by evening.

51
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:41,520
Right.

52
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:44,100
There, that's good.

53
00:03:44,920 --> 00:03:46,500
Ten bent a day!

54
00:03:47,240 --> 00:03:49,560
If I do say so myself,
what a brilliant idea.

55
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:51,920
That's dangerous, senpai.

56
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:53,920
I'm watching it properly, it's fine.

57
00:03:54,480 --> 00:03:56,840
You always say that and
then look away right away.

58
00:03:56,840 --> 00:03:57,680
That's right.

59
00:03:57,680 --> 00:04:01,480
Shut up, you two.
I said it's fine, so it's fine!

60
00:04:03,140 --> 00:04:14,000
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

61
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:17,020
Just because you're mad doesn't mean
you have to throw water on me too!

62
00:04:17,420 --> 00:04:18,740
Serves you right.

63
00:04:19,420 --> 00:04:21,860
Senpai. This is dangerous here.

64
00:04:21,910 --> 00:04:24,400
Why don't you use my break room?

65
00:04:24,880 --> 00:04:26,620
What a noisy bunch.

66
00:04:29,420 --> 00:04:30,700
Good grief, seriously.

67
00:04:31,460 --> 00:04:32,640
Reiko.

68
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:33,920
What now?

69
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:35,580
Hang this out to dry, will you?

70
00:04:35,720 --> 00:04:40,240
Damn it!
Why does Ryo-chan's clothing stink so much?

71
00:04:40,240 --> 00:04:44,680
Senpai has been wearing that same uniform nonstop for about ten years,
after all.

72
00:04:45,100 --> 00:04:47,600
No wonder you can't get girls.

73
00:04:50,760 --> 00:04:51,860
There, that should do.

74
00:04:53,620 --> 00:04:56,400
Reiko-san,
doesn't something smell like it's burning?

75
00:04:56,580 --> 00:04:58,260
Yes, I wonder what it is.

76
00:04:59,060 --> 00:04:59,980
No way.

77
00:04:59,980 --> 00:05:01,100
Senpai!

78
00:05:07,300 --> 00:05:08,940
What are you doing all of a sudden?

79
00:05:10,240 --> 00:05:11,020
That was a close one.

80
00:05:11,780 --> 00:05:13,400
Well, that's true.

81
00:05:13,860 --> 00:05:17,700
But, Reiko, what are these old
newspapers and magazines even for?

82
00:05:17,700 --> 00:05:22,060
The Chirigani exchange was supposed to come,
but they couldn't make it because of the snow.

83
00:05:22,060 --> 00:05:24,840
I put them here for the time
being and forgot about them.

84
00:05:24,840 --> 00:05:27,220
It's not all my fault, you know.

85
00:05:28,280 --> 00:05:30,440
Right, let's get back to work.

86
00:05:31,160 --> 00:05:33,480
Wait, wait, wait, hold on a second, senpai!

87
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:34,880
What now? Shut up, will you.

88
00:05:34,880 --> 00:05:37,480
This room is full of paper,
so it's dangerous.

89
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:39,540
Could you do it in the office instead?

90
00:05:43,320 --> 00:05:45,520
I've cleaned the break room.

91
00:05:45,520 --> 00:05:47,120
Sorry, Kei-chan.

92
00:05:48,100 --> 00:05:51,000
Ryo-chan, are you planning to
stay in that outfit the whole time?

93
00:05:51,140 --> 00:05:53,300
On a snowy day like this,
nobody's going to come.

94
00:05:53,300 --> 00:05:56,240
Besides, it was Reiko who told
me to do it here, wasn't it?

95
00:05:57,020 --> 00:05:58,360
Well, yeah, I suppose so.

96
00:06:03,940 --> 00:06:05,700
Well then, I've come to make the delivery.

97
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:09,460
Hey, don't lift it up so suddenly!

98
00:06:10,240 --> 00:06:10,720
It's freezing!

99
00:06:14,920 --> 00:06:17,730
Ryo-chan,

100
00:06:17,780 --> 00:06:20,640
Be careful!

101
00:06:20,960 --> 00:06:24,700
A candle flame won't set the
kerosene inside the can on fire.

102
00:06:25,260 --> 00:06:27,140
It's cold, so hurry up and close the bottom.

103
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:29,440
Yes! I'll bring it right in.

104
00:06:29,840 --> 00:06:33,340
I thought we only ordered one can.

105
00:06:33,660 --> 00:06:35,100
What? No, that can't be right.

106
00:06:36,020 --> 00:06:37,760
So this was the one-can order.

107
00:06:39,040 --> 00:06:41,680
I'm sorry, I went and brought seven cans.

108
00:06:42,920 --> 00:06:46,480
Well, fine then. Just leave them.
We'll need them anyway.

109
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:47,400
Sorry about that.

110
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:52,300
And since it's our tenth anniversary,
here are two more cans on the house.

111
00:06:55,020 --> 00:06:56,140
Thank you very much.

112
00:06:56,980 --> 00:06:57,720
My darling.

113
00:07:00,440 --> 00:07:01,800
Should we put them here?

114
00:07:02,400 --> 00:07:05,220
Because over there, Ryo-chan's using fire.

115
00:07:05,780 --> 00:07:07,900
This side is still safer.

116
00:07:07,900 --> 00:07:08,980
Yeah, that's right.

117
00:07:08,980 --> 00:07:12,660
But one wrong move and it'll
go up in flames in no time.

118
00:07:16,720 --> 00:07:17,760
Ryo-chan!

119
00:07:17,880 --> 00:07:19,540
I'll keep it in the break room,
far from here,

120
00:07:19,540 --> 00:07:21,600
but don't ever use fire over here.

121
00:07:22,220 --> 00:07:23,160
I know.

122
00:07:24,020 --> 00:07:27,748
Ryo-san, you there?

123
00:07:27,798 --> 00:07:30,160
Are you in?

124
00:07:30,460 --> 00:07:31,980
It's Honda.

125
00:07:32,400 --> 00:07:34,040
I'm busy right now.

126
00:07:35,220 --> 00:07:35,840
That's what I've been told, anyway.

127
00:07:36,520 --> 00:07:38,520
Could you hold on to my package for a bit?

128
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:40,480
It suddenly started pouring, you know.

129
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:42,060
If there's an accident, it'd be a disaster.

130
00:07:42,700 --> 00:07:43,980
Yes, that's fine.

131
00:07:43,980 --> 00:07:45,280
Right there, then.

132
00:07:46,340 --> 00:07:47,780
Excuse me.

133
00:07:49,880 --> 00:07:51,000
Don't tell me that's...

134
00:07:51,760 --> 00:07:52,640
Gasoline.

135
00:07:52,640 --> 00:07:53,860
Yes, it is.

136
00:07:54,480 --> 00:07:57,120
Honda, shut the door quickly, it's cold!

137
00:08:04,620 --> 00:08:08,140
Even a candle flame can set
the gasoline inside on fire.

138
00:08:09,020 --> 00:08:10,960
Anyway, I'm freezing.

139
00:08:11,340 --> 00:08:14,240
Sorry, we'll bring the rest right away.

140
00:08:16,320 --> 00:08:17,820
Is that all there is?

141
00:08:17,820 --> 00:08:22,280
The stand over there was selling them cheap,
so I went and bought them all in bulk.

142
00:08:26,820 --> 00:08:28,600
Quite the little fuel shop

143
00:08:28,600 --> 00:08:32,540
Unlike kerosene,
gasoline burns explosively, you know.

144
00:08:33,080 --> 00:08:36,220
If you mix them up and it ignites,
it'd be a disaster.

145
00:08:38,340 --> 00:08:42,420
Ryo-chan, absolutely, positively
do not use fire in the break room.

146
00:08:42,420 --> 00:08:43,940
I know.

147
00:08:47,800 --> 00:08:49,480
Finally, the second one's done!

148
00:08:50,080 --> 00:08:51,720
Alright, I'm going to keep making them!

149
00:08:55,180 --> 00:08:56,920
That sound was an accident.

150
00:09:02,180 --> 00:09:02,980
Are you all right?

151
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:06,320
Sorry, my tire slipped and

152
00:09:08,120 --> 00:09:10,380
is the road surface starting to freeze?

153
00:09:12,380 --> 00:09:14,340
Yes, that's all I need.

154
00:09:15,080 --> 00:09:18,900
Officer, I have a favor to ask.

155
00:09:19,300 --> 00:09:19,920
What is it?

156
00:09:20,400 --> 00:09:22,340
Could you hold a prisoner for us?

157
00:09:22,340 --> 00:09:24,700
With this snow,
it's dangerous to transport it,

158
00:09:24,700 --> 00:09:26,180
That's fine.

159
00:09:26,180 --> 00:09:27,220
What's the cargo?

160
00:09:28,100 --> 00:09:29,420
Dynamite.

161
00:09:29,420 --> 00:09:29,940
What?

162
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:35,620
It's apparently for use at a
construction site in Okuchichibu.

163
00:09:36,060 --> 00:09:38,080
With this snow,
the construction will be off too, won't it?

164
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:39,660
Ahaha, yes, that's right.

165
00:09:40,320 --> 00:09:41,640
So, is that just one box?

166
00:09:42,100 --> 00:09:44,360
No, there are 144 boxes.

167
00:09:44,360 --> 00:09:44,760
What?

168
00:09:45,460 --> 00:09:47,100
Hey, hurry up and shut it!

169
00:09:47,100 --> 00:09:48,400
I'm freezing!

170
00:09:54,320 --> 00:09:56,440
Be careful, senpai.

171
00:09:56,440 --> 00:09:58,020
It's dynamite!

172
00:09:58,580 --> 00:10:00,800
As long as the boxes don't catch fire,
we'll be fine.

173
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:02,360
We're not fine at all!

174
00:10:02,360 --> 00:10:05,020
Then I'll come pick them
up once the snow stops.

175
00:10:07,900 --> 00:10:08,840
This is trouble.

176
00:10:10,520 --> 00:10:13,600
The break room is full of old newspapers,
bean oil, and gasoline,

177
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:15,460
and now it's full of dynamite too!

178
00:10:16,260 --> 00:10:19,140
If it were to catch fire by mistake...

179
00:10:24,300 --> 00:10:28,260
Ryo-chan, you absolutely, positively,
definitely have to be careful with fire, okay?

180
00:10:28,260 --> 00:10:30,280
I already told you I know, didn't I?

181
00:10:31,180 --> 00:10:33,360
You're all making such a
racket I can't concentrate!

182
00:10:34,740 --> 00:10:35,680
There, that's good.

183
00:10:37,540 --> 00:10:38,800
Excuse me, sorry.

184
00:10:40,320 --> 00:10:41,400
Yes, what is it?

185
00:10:41,400 --> 00:10:45,380
Would it be all right if we parked our
truck somewhere behind the police box?

186
00:10:45,820 --> 00:10:48,720
If we keep going like this,
we're going to get stuck in the snow.

187
00:10:49,420 --> 00:10:50,920
I know we really shouldn't...

188
00:10:51,300 --> 00:10:53,440
Well, if that's the case,
I suppose there's no choice.

189
00:10:54,180 --> 00:10:54,830
Thank goodness.

190
00:10:54,880 --> 00:10:58,380
With what it is,
we can't just leave it in any old spot.

191
00:10:58,680 --> 00:11:01,940
Wait, is that truck carrying something?

192
00:11:02,260 --> 00:11:05,280
Yes. It's a tanker fully
loaded with natural gas.

193
00:11:05,640 --> 00:11:07,720
Hey, everyone, get out of here!

194
00:11:09,780 --> 00:11:11,620
Isn't it just one truck?

195
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:19,060
Kerosene, gasoline, and dynamite?

196
00:11:19,420 --> 00:11:22,760
And on top of that,
a tanker full of natural gas.

197
00:11:24,180 --> 00:11:25,500
If it catches fire by mistake,

198
00:11:28,100 --> 00:11:30,040
No, I don't even want to imagine it.

199
00:11:30,040 --> 00:11:31,700
Reiko, calm down.

200
00:11:32,680 --> 00:11:34,460
I'm leaving early today.

201
00:11:34,460 --> 00:11:34,820
What?

202
00:11:34,820 --> 00:11:36,560
Don't stop me, Ketcher!

203
00:11:43,560 --> 00:11:45,660
Isn't it a mountain of matches?

204
00:11:46,140 --> 00:11:48,420
Senpai, what on earth is all this?

205
00:11:49,960 --> 00:11:52,600
I thought they might be
worth something someday.

206
00:11:54,180 --> 00:11:54,980
They're old matches.

207
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:58,040
Those are just the boxes, right?
Say that's right, Ryo-chan.

208
00:11:58,600 --> 00:12:02,180
No, a collection only counts if
the contents are still in them.

209
00:12:02,980 --> 00:12:05,680
There are about two cardboard
boxes in the closet in the back, too.

210
00:12:06,620 --> 00:12:10,420
The back? You mean the break room packed full,
right above the dynamite?

211
00:12:26,480 --> 00:12:27,840
This music...

212
00:12:33,660 --> 00:12:36,200
Just as I thought, Colonel Bakuryū.

213
00:12:36,200 --> 00:12:44,020
Alright, I can see it now,
the Kōen-mae police box.

214
00:12:44,020 --> 00:12:47,580
I'll give them a nice greeting shot,
how about that.

215
00:12:47,580 --> 00:12:48,480
Do it.

216
00:12:48,960 --> 00:12:49,740
Roger.

217
00:13:25,420 --> 00:13:26,420
Ni, ni

218
00:13:29,060 --> 00:13:31,540
How about that? My playful greeting.

219
00:13:32,340 --> 00:13:35,280
Long time no see, you lot from Kōen-mae.

220
00:13:35,280 --> 00:13:38,540
I-I thought my heart was going to stop!

221
00:13:40,480 --> 00:13:42,660
Speaking of which, where's Ryotsu?

222
00:13:43,400 --> 00:13:46,780
The usually noisy man
is unusually quiet today.

223
00:13:47,370 --> 00:13:48,560
What is he doing?

224
00:13:48,700 --> 00:13:52,080
Shut up! I'm busy! Don't talk to me!

225
00:13:53,620 --> 00:13:58,420
Wh-what! Nobody has ever spoken to
me like that and got away with it!

226
00:13:58,780 --> 00:13:59,160
Yes, sir!

227
00:14:01,100 --> 00:14:04,760
If you fire right now and it ignites...

228
00:14:06,200 --> 00:14:08,280
Whoa! Colonel Bakuryu, please stop!

229
00:14:08,640 --> 00:14:11,080
We'll apologize for Ryo-chan's rudeness!

230
00:14:11,340 --> 00:14:14,120
You lot,
you really care about Ryotsu that much...

231
00:14:14,120 --> 00:14:15,020
Y-yes!

232
00:14:15,340 --> 00:14:16,500
So, please!

233
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:18,480
Yeah, got it!

234
00:14:21,100 --> 00:14:23,100
Thank you! Colonel Bakuryu!

235
00:14:23,800 --> 00:14:26,500
Pretending to stop, then shooting anyway!

236
00:14:30,200 --> 00:14:31,920
And it's really just a lighter!

237
00:14:34,280 --> 00:14:36,040
Don't scare us like that, Colonel!

238
00:14:36,340 --> 00:14:39,600
But if you make the flame bigger,
it becomes a flamethrower!

239
00:14:46,560 --> 00:14:47,980
Too bad, the gas ran out.

240
00:14:49,300 --> 00:14:52,420
What exactly did you come here for,
Colonel Bakuryu?

241
00:14:52,420 --> 00:14:56,580
Actually, I was just about to head
to the military training ground,

242
00:14:56,580 --> 00:15:00,340
but with this blizzard,
flying the helicopter is becoming dangerous.

243
00:15:00,820 --> 00:15:04,560
You're not going to ask us to handle a military helicopter,
are you?

244
00:15:04,560 --> 00:15:06,660
I wouldn't be so shameless as to say that.

245
00:15:06,660 --> 00:15:09,320
I just need you to keep some
weapons and ammunition for me.

246
00:15:09,600 --> 00:15:10,520
Unique!

247
00:15:13,380 --> 00:15:15,040
N-no way, that's ridiculous.

248
00:15:21,120 --> 00:15:24,660
Kameari Park police box,
I thank you all for your cooperation.

249
00:15:24,660 --> 00:15:26,420
Well then, farewell!

250
00:15:34,380 --> 00:15:35,900
W-what should we do?

251
00:15:36,140 --> 00:15:37,740
What do you mean, what should we do?

252
00:15:39,600 --> 00:15:42,140
Up there there's a huge stash of
US military weapons and ammunition,

253
00:15:42,780 --> 00:15:46,280
and a tanker truck full of
natural gas is surrounding us.

254
00:15:46,620 --> 00:15:50,580
The break room is packed with dynamite,
kerosene, and gasoline too.

255
00:15:50,580 --> 00:15:53,460
And now Colonel Bakuryu's
weapons are here too.

256
00:15:56,380 --> 00:15:58,400
I can't take it anymore, I can't stand this!

257
00:15:58,940 --> 00:16:01,620
Kei-chan, let's both leave early after all!

258
00:16:02,220 --> 00:16:03,380
Reiko-san, calm down!

259
00:16:03,900 --> 00:16:06,293
If we run away from here,

260
00:16:06,343 --> 00:16:08,420
Senpai will be left here all alone!

261
00:16:11,700 --> 00:16:14,760
What do you think will happen to
Senpai if we leave him like this?

262
00:16:23,980 --> 00:16:27,600
If that happens, everything within several
hundred meters will definitely be blown away.

263
00:16:27,940 --> 00:16:31,220
Kei-chan, let's just stop
Ryo-chan from making that birdcage.

264
00:16:32,520 --> 00:16:36,360
The senpai has nothing on his mind right
now but the 500,000 yen from the birdcage.

265
00:16:37,060 --> 00:16:41,080
Do you think he'll listen
to us when money is involved?

266
00:16:47,040 --> 00:16:47,606
Well, no,

267
00:16:47,656 --> 00:16:51,200
there's no point talking
to Ryo-chan right now. But!

268
00:16:52,800 --> 00:16:54,888
We mustn't panic, Reiko-san.

269
00:16:54,938 --> 00:16:58,680
If we don't keep our heads here,
we can't protect the peace of Kameari!

270
00:16:59,920 --> 00:17:03,740
Alright, Kei-chan.
Then I'll go put some tea on.

271
00:17:10,260 --> 00:17:10,960
Reiko-san!

272
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:20,960
Something's burning.

273
00:17:20,960 --> 00:17:23,100
Kei-chan, something's scorching!

274
00:17:27,140 --> 00:17:39,980
!

275
00:17:39,980 --> 00:17:40,940
It suddenly got cold

276
00:17:41,540 --> 00:17:43,240
Oh no, my uniform!

277
00:17:43,800 --> 00:17:45,820
Sorry, I was careless.

278
00:17:45,820 --> 00:17:46,940
And the stove, too.

279
00:17:46,940 --> 00:17:49,360
Once it's in that state,
you can't use it anymore, you know.

280
00:17:49,360 --> 00:17:51,260
I'll go get a replacement.

281
00:17:51,840 --> 00:17:52,680
Hurry up.

282
00:17:55,360 --> 00:17:57,180
Now, now, what should we do?

283
00:17:57,640 --> 00:17:59,320
I'll go buy something for you to wear.

284
00:17:59,320 --> 00:18:01,060
Kei-chan, bring the stove.

285
00:18:01,540 --> 00:18:02,220
Understood.

286
00:18:02,220 --> 00:18:05,960
But it's dangerous for both of us to leave the police box at once,
isn't it?

287
00:18:06,480 --> 00:18:06,840
That's true.

288
00:18:07,660 --> 00:18:08,440
This is a problem.

289
00:18:11,160 --> 00:18:12,220
Maria-chan

290
00:18:12,220 --> 00:18:13,060
Hi there

291
00:18:13,980 --> 00:18:14,800
What's up?

292
00:18:15,160 --> 00:18:17,740
I came by to direct traffic near here,

293
00:18:17,740 --> 00:18:20,180
but the roads are blocked by snow.

294
00:18:20,800 --> 00:18:23,160
Reiko-san, perfect timing!

295
00:18:23,160 --> 00:18:23,880
Yeah, I suppose.

296
00:18:24,360 --> 00:18:26,940
Maria-chan, I have a little favor to ask.

297
00:18:27,540 --> 00:18:29,280
While we're out for a bit,

298
00:18:29,280 --> 00:18:31,440
make sure Ryo-chan doesn't
do anything dangerous.

299
00:18:31,440 --> 00:18:32,960
Could you keep an eye on him?

300
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:35,180
Alone with Ryo-sama?

301
00:18:35,180 --> 00:18:36,760
Yes, I'd be delighted!

302
00:18:40,260 --> 00:18:42,380
Maria-chan, then I'm counting on you.

303
00:18:42,380 --> 00:18:42,720
Yes.

304
00:18:43,600 --> 00:18:44,880
Let's hurry, Kei-chan.

305
00:18:44,880 --> 00:18:45,660
Yes.

306
00:18:55,200 --> 00:18:56,063
It's snowing outside,

307
00:18:56,113 --> 00:18:59,540
and it's just Ryo-sama and me, all alone.

308
00:19:00,080 --> 00:19:02,300
Isn't that romantic?

309
00:19:03,100 --> 00:19:05,720
Hey, Ryo-sama, since we're finally alone,

310
00:19:06,760 --> 00:19:07,440
shall we do something together?

311
00:19:10,080 --> 00:19:15,840
If it's that Mass-Produced one, she's so annoying!
I'm busy! Mass-Produced types are so mean.

312
00:19:15,840 --> 00:19:23,840
Right, I brought something really wonderful!
The Mass-Produced one will be happy too, I'm sure. Ta-da!

313
00:19:24,360 --> 00:19:27,940
Fireworks! Winter fireworks are so romantic,
don't you think?

314
00:19:30,240 --> 00:19:31,140
Do whatever you want.

315
00:19:31,760 --> 00:19:32,560
Okay~

316
00:19:35,740 --> 00:19:38,140
Will the police box be all right?

317
00:19:38,140 --> 00:19:40,300
I haven't seen any fire
trucks or patrol cars,

318
00:19:40,300 --> 00:19:42,020
so it's probably fine, I'd think.

319
00:19:42,440 --> 00:19:45,680
I just can't shake the worry
unless I see it with my own eyes.

320
00:19:48,940 --> 00:19:50,620
We're fine, Reiko-san.

321
00:19:50,620 --> 00:19:51,540
Thank goodness.

322
00:19:52,040 --> 00:19:54,920
Maria-chan,
you really kept an eye on Ryo-chan for us.

323
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:56,920
Come on, let's hurry and go.

324
00:20:02,280 --> 00:20:03,220
Ahahaha!

325
00:20:04,720 --> 00:20:06,820
Ryo-sama, look, look!

326
00:20:07,220 --> 00:20:08,740
So pretty!

327
00:20:08,940 --> 00:20:09,760
You hate these, don't you?

328
00:20:10,540 --> 00:20:11,300
No way!

329
00:20:11,620 --> 00:20:12,480
Aaaaaah!

330
00:20:13,040 --> 00:20:14,340
No, no, no!

331
00:20:14,680 --> 00:20:16,120
Maria-chan, stop!

332
00:20:16,900 --> 00:20:19,520
Why are you setting off
fireworks inside the room?

333
00:20:19,760 --> 00:20:21,520
Because it's cold outside.

334
00:20:21,580 --> 00:20:25,160
Maria-chan, take a good look at the room.

335
00:20:29,220 --> 00:20:30,640
Reiko, this is...

336
00:20:30,640 --> 00:20:34,520
By the way, there's some in the
break room and on the roof too.

337
00:20:34,520 --> 00:20:34,920
What?

338
00:20:35,640 --> 00:20:38,300
If she's setting off fireworks, that's
a disaster waiting to happen, isn't it?

339
00:20:38,300 --> 00:20:40,400
Exactly, that's why I stopped her!

340
00:20:42,760 --> 00:20:44,820
Yes, this is Kōen-mae
Station departing, but...

341
00:20:44,820 --> 00:20:46,280
I'll put him on right away.

342
00:20:46,280 --> 00:20:48,340
Senpai, you have a call.

343
00:20:48,340 --> 00:20:49,680
What?

344
00:20:50,180 --> 00:20:51,000
Hello?

345
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:52,500
It's the birdcage shop.

346
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:53,900
What?

347
00:20:56,220 --> 00:20:58,100
I mean, with this heavy snow today, right?

348
00:20:58,100 --> 00:20:59,920
There's no way I can go pick it up, so...

349
00:20:59,920 --> 00:21:02,500
Let's just say we'll
pick it up tomorrow, okay?

350
00:21:02,500 --> 00:21:03,060
Hey, wait.

351
00:21:03,060 --> 00:21:03,780
Well, then.

352
00:21:05,940 --> 00:21:06,740
Damn it.

353
00:21:06,740 --> 00:21:08,580
Forget it, forget it.

354
00:21:10,020 --> 00:21:11,140
Honestly...

355
00:21:12,620 --> 00:21:14,000
Well, that's a relief.

356
00:21:14,480 --> 00:21:14,880
Yeah, right.

357
00:21:19,440 --> 00:21:21,200
Doesn't something smell weird?

358
00:21:21,600 --> 00:21:23,140
Isn't it the smell of fireworks?

359
00:21:24,300 --> 00:21:25,800
I don't think so, though.

360
00:21:26,860 --> 00:21:30,040
That's probably from when
Senpai just blew out the candle.

361
00:21:30,040 --> 00:21:31,300
Yeah, probably.

362
00:21:32,060 --> 00:21:34,760
Ryo-chan, did you give up on
making the birdcage already?

363
00:21:35,060 --> 00:21:39,000
Shut up!
Damn it, I worked so hard making it!

364
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:42,780
Scary. Better not mess with him, then.

365
00:21:45,880 --> 00:21:47,380
Shall we take a little break?

366
00:21:47,840 --> 00:21:49,820
Agreed! I'll make some tea.

367
00:21:49,820 --> 00:21:51,120
I'll help.

368
00:21:51,680 --> 00:21:52,620
Then I'll help too.

369
00:21:53,220 --> 00:21:56,460
The gas is already on, isn't it?

370
00:21:56,460 --> 00:21:59,780
Danger! I forgot I left it running!

371
00:22:00,520 --> 00:22:03,560
This is bad! The flame's out!
Gas is building up!

372
00:22:04,180 --> 00:22:05,280
The ventilation fan!

373
00:22:05,520 --> 00:22:05,820
No, you mustn't!

374
00:22:06,900 --> 00:22:09,800
The fan switch could
make sparks and ignite it!

375
00:22:10,280 --> 00:22:11,560
Then what should we do?

376
00:22:12,140 --> 00:22:13,640
First, slowly open the window...

377
00:22:15,980 --> 00:22:18,820
Let's quietly and slowly get away from here.

378
00:22:19,980 --> 00:22:20,960
Thank you for your hard work.

379
00:22:22,800 --> 00:22:25,040
What, you came all the way out
here on a snowy day like this?

380
00:22:25,040 --> 00:22:26,580
You're a damn serious one, aren't you.

381
00:22:26,580 --> 00:22:27,980
It's technically work, after all.

382
00:22:28,420 --> 00:22:30,400
Ryo-san, what are you doing naked?

383
00:22:30,400 --> 00:22:31,480
All sorts of things.

384
00:22:33,180 --> 00:22:35,260
Ryo-san, don't you smell?

385
00:22:35,880 --> 00:22:38,840
Maria was setting off
fireworks in here just now.

386
00:22:39,220 --> 00:22:41,120
And I was lighting candles too.

387
00:22:41,540 --> 00:22:42,180
So that's it.

388
00:22:42,740 --> 00:22:43,640
Right, Ryo-san.

389
00:22:44,160 --> 00:22:46,280
I can do that now too.

390
00:22:46,280 --> 00:22:47,980
Do what?

391
00:22:48,500 --> 00:22:51,120
The thing you did at the year-end party.

392
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:52,900
I practiced, and now I can do it.

393
00:22:52,900 --> 00:22:54,220
That.

394
00:22:54,740 --> 00:22:55,780
Alright, go ahead and try it.

395
00:22:55,780 --> 00:22:56,920
I'll watch you.

396
00:22:56,920 --> 00:22:57,360
Yeah.

397
00:22:57,920 --> 00:23:00,220
It's a good thing Ryo-chan put out the fire.

398
00:23:00,580 --> 00:23:03,700
If that had caught fire,
it would have been a disaster.

399
00:23:04,320 --> 00:23:08,480
We need to warn the senior officer not to use
any flames until the gas is completely gone.

400
00:23:08,940 --> 00:23:09,580
Senior officer!

401
00:23:12,120 --> 00:23:13,500
Here goes, Ryo-san.

402
00:23:15,100 --> 00:23:17,700
Alright, go on then,
light your fart on fire and show us.

403
00:23:22,500 --> 00:23:23,760
Aaaaaah!

404
00:23:23,760 --> 00:23:24,640
Aaaaaah!

405
00:23:43,420 --> 00:23:47,100
Terai, your fart is far too powerful!

406
00:23:47,100 --> 00:23:49,060
S-sorry!

407
00:23:49,060 --> 00:23:51,980
This has turned into the
worst possible situation.

408
00:23:51,980 --> 00:23:55,760
W-why does this always happen?

409
00:24:15,420 --> 00:24:17,700
Surprised and making a ruckus,

410
00:24:17,700 --> 00:24:20,600
solving together, and resolving it,

411
00:24:20,600 --> 00:24:23,640
quickly, and helping out,

412
00:24:24,640 --> 00:24:35,360
swiftly, decided, with inspiration and bounce,
gathered together, taking action and flying off,

413
00:24:36,140 --> 00:24:39,740
more than anything, incredible power,

414
00:24:39,740 --> 00:24:45,880
everyone gather, if you come here,

415
00:24:46,840 --> 00:24:52,240
like a dream, the final energy.

416
00:24:53,560 --> 00:24:59,620
Gaze at tomorrow, believe in yesterday, paint
the universe, and if you stand on the ground,

417
00:24:59,620 --> 00:25:03,400
the star of Kameari spun
around and drew a circle.

418
00:25:05,600 --> 00:25:07,080
This is good enough, right?

419
00:25:07,080 --> 00:25:08,540
No way it's good enough, idiot.

420
00:25:21,620 --> 00:25:26,320
What? They discovered an antibody in
my body that keeps out any disease?

421
00:25:26,760 --> 00:25:30,420
So if they can make a medicine that works on anything from it,
that's a Nobel Prize-worthy thing

422
00:25:30,960 --> 00:25:33,340
That means I'm a treasure
of the world, then.

423
00:25:33,720 --> 00:25:36,460
Next time: Leap, Ryotsu GPX.

424
00:25:36,960 --> 00:25:37,540
See you then.

